<Career id="ARCH1-WORK96">
<Description language="ENGLISH">"Fieldwarden"</Description>
<Explanation language="ENGLISH">"Halflings prefer militias to standing armies, and have little apparent military strength to those unfamiliar with their ways. Visitors to the Moot often wonder at how the countryside and villages remain so peaceful and idyllic despite sharing a border with dread Sylvania where the dead never rest, with no obvious armies to repel them. A large part of the credit for this goes to the Field Wardens. These brave halflings patrol the borders of the Moot, using their intimate knowledge of the terrain and cunning guerrilla tactics to deter unwanted visitors. A Field Warden is first and foremost a Halfling of the people, a friendly face to reassure the public that all is well. They know every family in their area (and which baked treats they are likely to serve a Field Warden who happens to be passing by around tea time). It is a highly respected position, and any Field Warden can expect a busy off-duty calendar as families invite them to Bakeday meals, wedding feasts, funeral remembrance dinners or pie eating competitions."</Explanation>
